e":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T16:32:23-07:00","id":1418117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1418113#post1418113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, definitely not the same as Mexico by Night</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it was based on it though. Lots of information from it.<br /> <br /> Mexico City by Night remains one of my favorite books.<br /> <br /> Glad it got an update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T05:23:12-07:00","id":1418176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1418117#post1418117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it was based on it though. Lots of information from it.<br /> <br /> Mexico City by Night remains one of my favorite books.<br /> <br /> Glad it got an update.</div> </div> </div> </div>can't share the sentiment,<br /> Mexico by Night had alot of potential for giving the sabbat a breath of fresh air,<br /> <br /> the UC promised a a more centralised sabbat, lead by strong leaders, the lasombra ideal with more involvement in mortal affairs,<br /> <br /> the Moderates promised an end to the crusades, more space for personal development under the umbrella of powerful Tzimisce,<br /> <br /> and the Status Quo was just the old sabbat we knew and loved, with less restraints on the antitribu<br /> <br /> a new sabbat for new horrors, new conflicts and new crushed dreams<br /> <br /> BJD and V5 didn't really follow up on this, they just went &quot;everything went to shit for the sabbat, now they have to start over from square one&quot;,<br /> even the Loyalists didn't get what they wanted<br /> <br /> there's also some stuff in MCbN that I feel needed to be more coverage, like the blood cults","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T06:31:34-07:00","id":1418182,"title":"","content":"Honestly I imagined the UC to be the 'you need to chill out bro' extreme of the Sabbat. Like, the loyalists are the equivelant of communists we-need-to-shut-down so the UC should rightly be the Incel-fascists. &quot;Reasonable&quot; discorse should really be between the moderates, status quo and orthodoxy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T08:01:35-07:00","id":1418189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1418182#post1418182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I imagined the UC to be the 'you need to chill out bro' extreme of the Sabbat. Like, the loyalists are the equivelant of communists we-need-to-shut-down so the UC should rightly be the Incel-fascists. &quot;Reasonable&quot; discorse should really be between the moderates, status quo and orthodoxy.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol, I sure wouldn't call the moderates &quot;reasonable&quot;,<br /> they def have some reasonable policies, but their supporters and leaders are also complete degens who want more space to indulge their degeneracy<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T08:18:08-07:00","id":1418191,"title":"","content":"It's too late for the Sabbat.<br /> The only chance of continued 'survival' for vampiric society was keeping humans enslaved and stupid.<br /> The masquerade only prolonged the inevitable and it was only a matter of time before it blew up.<br /> Meanwhile it gave mortal society opportunity to evolve and develop the technological means to beat the kindred.<br /> If vampiric society wanted to keep humans as herds and limited, they should have done so long before. <br /> Once the industrial age broke through, there was no more turning of the tide.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T10:55:32-07:00","id":1418555,"title":"","content":"I never Liked the Sabbat, there just a bunch of Edgelord bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T09:34:08-08:00","id":1425750,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, because of how the Sabbat is, they likely won't survive long if they were in charge because of a combination of hubris and infighting. The Camarilla is all about secrecy and self preservation when it comes to dealing with humanity. Sabbat believe they are the masters of humanity and will be too prideful to have the necessary restraint needed to survive the Second Inquisition. So more cities controlled by the Sabbat will simply mean more cities with mysterious 'terrorist cells' that need to be taken out by special forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T10:25:47-08:00","id":1425759,"title":"","content":"As others have said, the Sabbat aren't inherently that united except by having the Camarilla as their enemy. They likely don't have the organizational structure to resist fracturing if they win. You also have an assortment of different factions and ideologies within the Sabbat, some of which includes some pretty crazy ideas which would cause mayhem if they tries to implement them unopposed. If the Camarilla were truly crushed by the Sabbat, the Sabbat would actually have to recreate something like the Camarilla. The more intelligent and rational Sabbat, including the powerful and influential elders, would have to reign in some of the craziness of the Sect. They would need to increase their power over the mortal world, control; more politicians, get more money, make more ghouls - they would need to do this to fill the vacuum of the Camarilla and to preserve the Masquerade which they would have to do if they're sane. They would also have to enforce the Masquerade on individual packs, they can't just have some random nomadic Sabbat packs running around using their powers in public, because it is their influential elders who would have to scramble to cover it up. We see a new Camarilla emerging here, with those who oppose those activities becoming the new Sabbat. There's no way that all of the Camarilla vampires would be dead in this scenario, many would have been driven into hiding, forced to join the Sabbat, or simply become independent. If the more level headed Sabbat elders start becoming more like the Camarilla, they might be able to get the support of formerly Camarilla vampires. <br /> <br /> To the degree that the Sabbat win and still maintain their character as the Sabbat, a lot of problems will arise. There will be more Masquerade breeches and that doesn't only concern vampires, it is also a problem for other supernatural creatures who want to keep the existence of supernatural creatures a secret. For the most part, mages leave vampires alone, but if most vampires were the Sabbat, who callously kill mortals on a whim, who play fast and loose with the Masquerade, who mass embrace mortals in times of need - that might be something that would call for more direct intervention from the Technocracy, even from Tradition mages too. Werewolves might be more inclines to go into cities to fight vampires too if the vampires are now all super Wyrm tainted and are killing humans in droves. Other supernaturals might get involved too.,<br /> <br /> Ignoring other gamelines for a moment, the more reckless and murderous vampires behave (which includes the Sabbat unless the more rational elders can reign them in) the more human hunters there will be and the more resources they will be willing to bring to bear against Sabbat vampires. The ultimate example being an end to the Masquerade and a war between humanity and the Sabbat. Of course, other vampires aren't going to like that idea, so back to a new Camarilla forming, it may be the case that independent Clans and bloodlines might have to join together to oppose the Sabbat, in fact they might even start doing that before the Camarilla falls when it looks like the Sabbat is winning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T17:42:55-08:00","id":1425814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1417836#post1417836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would probably then get smoked by humanity when they decided it's time to rule over the cattle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is basically my answer. The Sabbat is a lot more blatant and open about their condition than the Camarilla, and once the Camarilla is defeated, the Sabbat have one less reason to keep hidden and to a degree, keep working with one another. I would imagine they they end up getting into some nasty factional fights civil/war and the end result is, humanity finds out about the existence of vampires even faster, and the Second Inquisition ramps up even faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:09:31-08:00","id":1425987,"title":"","content":"Ironically, if the Sabbat were to survive after becoming the dominant force, they'd have to embrace secrecy and structure, exercise restraint, and come up with a set of core rules and principles that all vampires must follow to ensure their survival. Basically, they would become the new Camarilla, lol.<br /> <br /> Note that the whole humanity thing is not a Camarilla principle. The Camarilla doesn't give two sh*ts about being humane and are perfectly fine with their members being total monsters ... as long as said monsters are subtle, secretive, and respect authority. If one of their own wishes to kidnap a couple of humans to gleefully torture and mentally fracture, all the power to them. As long it doesn't draw unwanted attention their way from other humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:16:08-08:00","id":1425991,"title":"","content":"My Camarilla vampires will totally use your lack of humanity to persecute or socially condemn you. <br /> They'll also despise you for having high humanity... <br /> <br /> <br /> I think if the Sabbat did take over they'd just lay low and prepare for the war. Most of their masquerade breaks are weaponized utility, not something they'd casually do in their own back yard. If you're going to live in packs, you're eventually going to get fed up with any excessive bullshit that could bring the hunts down on ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T17:11:41-08:00","id":1426507,"title":"","content":"The best Sabbat Ascension scenario I've ever seen was described in Dark Ages V20 Apocrypha of the Clans, Salubri section. Every single line of it is amazing. Once, I will certainly do a chronicle based on this alternative.<br /> I still think that Salubri always would make an amazing third leg for the Sabbat's chair at its foundation, countering the two Douche clans' predatory politics and overall being the 'adult in the room' for the sect, helping to (repeatedly) root out infernalism and sneaky stabbers like TMR and to convert the ideology of Sabbat regarding mortals from indiscriminate abuse towards efficient parasitism. If only they could pull their stuff together back then in dark ages and join Tzimisce in their war before the Revolt. A man can dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T19:49:21-08:00","id":1426523,"title":"","content":"A Sabbat with the Salubri among its founders would have been the enemy the Tremere really deserved.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, Salubri with allies. The fact that no one raised a finger to help a clan that would have basically been everyone's second best ally, or to stop a clearly ambitious and deadly school of bloodthirsty newcomers, always made more sense as a deliberately tragic emotional narrative on the real life publisher's part than as a tactical move on the Kindred's part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T04:09:08-08:00","id":1426559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426523#post1426523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sabbat with the Salubri among its founders would have been the enemy the Tremere really deserved.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, Salubri with allies. The fact that no one raised a finger to help a clan that would have basically been everyone's second best ally, or to stop a clearly ambitious and deadly school of bloodthirsty newcomers, always made more sense as a deliberately tragic emotional narrative on the real life publisher's part than as a tactical move on the Kindred's part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would anyone help a Clan that got upstaged so easily for? That doesn't make sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T04:25:09-08:00","id":1426561,"title":"","content":"Nobody wanted to help the Salubri because it was in their best interest not to help the Salubri. Few clans cared for the Salubri, nobody trusted the Salubri, and many people owed the Salubri favours, but having one-way debt? If someone comes along with a promise of wiping away your debt, who can also grant impressive favours, and also they'll blacklist you if you get in the way, would you really be backing the Salubri? <br /> <br /> The Salubri, even more than the later capadocians, were just destined to be wiped out, like any other Dark-Age Bloodline that also got wiped. It's their own fault; a stupid weakness, a bad discipline spread for neonates, a poor attitude for working with others... Why would anyone bet on these guys over the Tremere, who, pre-v5, had only one weakness: being so overwhelmingly successful that it was pissing everyone else off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T04:28:01-08:00","id":1426562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426559#post1426559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why would anyone help a Clan that got upstaged so easily for? That doesn't make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Salubri aren't Tremere, that's reason enough for me,<br /> though &quot;help&quot; isn't in most vampires' lingo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T00:38:53-08:00","id":1426658,"title":"","content":"The Assamites were the closest thing to an ally the Salubri had, and the most they could do was help evacuate as many as they could east.<br /> <br /> And all <i>that </i>accomplished was putting Haqim's Children on the Tremere's shitlist. And probably setting the stage for their part in the Anarch Revolt (&quot;Hey you wanna come eat some elders oppressing us?&quot; &quot;Yeah after what kind of assholes they seemed to be last time we were around, we're down&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T03:17:41-08:00","id":1426673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426658#post1426658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Assamites were the closest thing to an ally the Salubri had, and the most they could do was help evacuate as many as they could east.<br /> <br /> And all <i>that </i>accomplished was putting Haqim's Children on the Tremere's shitlist. And probably setting the stage for their part in the Anarch Revolt (&quot;Hey you wanna come eat some elders oppressing us?&quot; &quot;Yeah after what kind of assholes they seemed to be last time we were around, we're down&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>and now they are in the Camarilla with the Tremere, just like the Nosferatu and, maybe soon, the Tzimisce<br /> <br /> so...yeah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T04:30:08-08:00","id":1426681,"title":"","content":"Oh god Tzimisce in the Camarilla would be hilarious. Even the Assamite hateboner for the Warlocks paled in comparison (as much as a third of the clan was willing to set that... uh, boner aside in the name of survival).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T05:14:07-08:00","id":1426684,"title":"","content":"Where is there any information of the Tzimisce joining (or hint) the Camarilla at all? The whole point of the deal-breaker of them considering joining was the fact that the Tremere were in it in the first place. Not only that their basic philosophies they abide by don't roll with the Camarilla. Can we please stop putting Clans that make no sense in the Camarilla into to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T05:31:48-08:00","id":1426689,"title":"","content":"Well since the Tremere are all dead I guess the tzmusce can join without any other reservations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T06:24:02-08:00","id":1426692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426684#post1426684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is there any information of the Tzimisce joining (or hint) the Camarilla at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>nowhere, except for the Tzimisce Prince in Tokyo,<br /> <br /> I'm just getting ready for the worst,<br /> it's been two years since the Lasombra and Assamite, you should be familiar with the V5 paradigm by now<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426689#post1426689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well since the Tremere are all dead I guess the tzmusce can join without any other reservations.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but emphasis on &quot;join&quot;,<br /> the Tzimisce I know and love wouldn't just &quot;join&quot;, they would conquer the Camarilla, clean up the Tremere filth and plaster Toreador skin as wallpaper,<br /> hopefully with the help of some Nosferatu who have been eager to bash in some Ventrue skulls since the Inquisition started<br /> <br /> but...that's not how V5 would handle it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T08:12:28-08:00","id":1426708,"title":"","content":"I don't see why one 12th generation Tzimisce in Tokyo in the 21st century should deeply care about a war in medieval Europe. If there's any Tzimisce figure V5 gritting their teeth about being in the same sect as House Tremere, it's the former prince of Tblisi, assuming her title infers membership of the Camarilla and even she could be part of a bloodline that had nothing to do with the Omen War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T08:52:58-08:00","id":1426712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">12th generation <b>Tzimisce in Tokyo</b> in the 21st century</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that this is even a thing really annoys me, much less that its a 12th gen Vampire that is somehow a Prince. And no, until there is a clear retcon (which I sure it will be with how this edition operates) almost all Tzimisce REALLY hate the Tremere for upfronting them all those ages ago. That's how Vampires operate, with long centuries old grudges that are even passed down to their childer. Besides, even barring that like I said before, the Tzimisce's philosophy and way of unlife are removed from the Camarilla completely. They'd have no desire to join this sect at all realistically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T09:40:56-08:00","id":1426717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426712#post1426712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that this is even a thing really annoys me, much less that its a 12th gen Vampire that is somehow a Prince. And no, until there is a clear retcon (which I sure it will be with how this edition operates) almost all Tzimisce REALLY hate the Tremere for upfronting them all those ages ago. That's how Vampires operate, with long centuries old grudges that are even passed down to their childer. Besides, even barring that like I said before, the Tzimisce's philosophy and way of unlife are removed from the Camarilla completely. They'd have no desire to join this sect at all realistically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curious what are your thoughts on Nagalopers? They don\u2019t seem to know much about nonAfrican Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T10:05:08-08:00","id":1426720,"title":"","content":"The Naglopers are a batch of Tzimisce that came about the Antediluvian itself during its initial travels around the world before settling down in Eastern Europe. Since they predate the start of the Tremere, they of course wouldn't have any animosity regarding them. Though still however, the Naglopers just as the European Tzimisce are very much alien and removed from human thought completely and seek different goals than what would be acceptable in the Camarilla; actually the Camarilla has no foothold in the African continent at all to begin with, so they wouldn't be able to join. Even then I'm not sure the Naglopers or any of the Laibon would want to join at all considering the shadow wars fought with the Cam during the colonial age (the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom say that while the African mortals lost in the motions of colonialism, parallel the Kindred societies of Africa won out- but with their herds changed and alien to them after colonialism ended).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T11:16:42-08:00","id":1426723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426720#post1426720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Naglopers are a batch of Tzimisce that came about the Antediluvian itself during its initial travels around the world before settling down in Eastern Europe. Since they predate the start of the Tremere, they of course wouldn't have any animosity regarding them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there can be an African bloodline of Tzimisce that split off before the antediluvian settled down Eastern Europe, then why can't there be one that spread to Japan? What about Kartarirya's descendants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T11:37:23-08:00","id":1426725,"title":"","content":"Because [Tzimisce] never went to East Asia, so there is no real batch of them aside from modern developments (which can be extrapolated due to the &quot;Prince&quot; of Tokyo being such a high generation). Tzimisce presence in Asia have been mostly in India at best. Maybe an Indian Tzimisce was the one to embrace that lady in Japan in the first place. Though it still begs the question on any answer to the Wan-Kuei if they are retconned or such, because East Asia and Southeast is literally their main spawning points and they've been fighting on and off with the Indian Kindred for a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T12:22:00-08:00","id":1426730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426725#post1426725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe an Indian Tzimisce was the one to embrace that lady in Japan in the first place. Though it still begs the question on any answer to the Wan-Kuei if they are retconned or such, because East Asia and Southeast is literally their main spawning points and they've been fighting on and off with the Indian Kindred for a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I think. That's why I brought up her generation. A Tzimisce methuselah is unlikely to be in Tokyo, but there are nine degrees of separation between [Tzimisce] and Shibasaki. The Wan-Kuei in V5 are another question, which I amongst others have asked on this forum before, and I don't expect a published answer any time soon.<br /> <br /> By the way, you're correct to call her '&quot;Prince&quot;'. <i>Camarilla</i> says &quot;she doesn't rule, technically, but ensures order is kept and tribute flows upstream&quot;. She's a <i>de facto</i> prince at best. Given that Tokyo's elders &quot;are expected to relocate to Kyoto&quot; for some undisclosed reason, she could be authorised by figures further &quot;upstream&quot;, in the latter city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T12:29:28-08:00","id":1426731,"title":"","content":"Well the Tremere are all dead. Just call slap 'house Carna' onto the logo of the survivors and the Tzmisce will think they're a totaly different, totally cool organization they can live with in peace. <br /> <br /> In seriousness. I don't think the Tzmisce would join the Camarilla even if God turned the Tremere to blood and sucked them up into the sun. A lot of Camarilla elders really, really, really hate Vicissitude, for reasons both reasonable and wildly imaginative. <br /> <br /> But I suppose that's gonna become Protean, or if we're really &quot;lucky&quot;, it'll be Blood Sorcery. Neither of which are all that terrifying. So, in the end, the Tzmisce will just join the Camarilla like there's never been anything wrong with that. The Salubri too. And the Ravnos because We-'re-definately-not-racist.. Or maybe they'll join the Anarchs because that's the cool kids club. All the clans will nicely fit into team A or Team Cam; all the nonsensical barriers that kept them apart will be eroded. Of course the Clan of death and the various bloodlines they've absorbed will be their own thing because someone thought it'd be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T14:08:19-08:00","id":1426737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426731#post1426731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I suppose that's gonna become Protean, or if we're really &quot;lucky&quot;, it'll be Blood Sorcery. Neither of which are all that terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm going to shape you into some sort of hound creature-&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh no!&quot;<br /> &quot;-using Protean.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, that's a relief, I thought I was going to have a problem.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T14:32:29-08:00","id":1426744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426737#post1426737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I'm going to shape you into some sort of hound creature-&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh no!&quot;<br /> &quot;-using Protean.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, that's a relief, I thought I was going to have a problem.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if this joke's meant to be interpreted at my expense, so I feel I should clarify: Yes, that's exactly how it is. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude is magic surgery. <br /> Protean metaphysically is just... using the beast to make temporary transformations. It's the standard magic shapeshifting If I someone somehow turned you into a dog with protean (It's a very personal power you can only use on yourself, but never mind that) you'd expect to transform back without any hassle at some point. <br /> If someone transformed me into a hound with monster-surgery... yeah, that's not something you recover from. The difference is night and day. The literal meanings of the words 'protean' and 'vicissitude' imply very different things too. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T14:43:36-08:00","id":1426746,"title":"","content":"As an aside, i find it hilarious that the Tzimisce bloodline in Africa are called &quot;Naglopers&quot;. Thats Afrikaans for &quot;Nightwalker&quot;. It's like when Stephen King thought &quot;Boomslang&quot; was a cool name for a species of snake so he came up with &quot;Peruvian Boomslang&quot;, which is double hilarious when you discover Boomslang is just Afrikaans for &quot;Tree Snake&quot;.<br /> <br /> Man i am glad for the internet, it makes research so much easier so you avoid little mistakes like these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T14:58:01-08:00","id":1426747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426744#post1426744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this joke's meant to be interpreted at my expense, so I feel I should clarify: Yes, that's exactly how it is.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is magic surgery.<br /> Protean metaphysically is just... using the beast to make temporary transformations. It's the standard magic shapeshifting If I someone somehow turned you into a dog with protean (It's a very personal power you can only use on yourself, but never mind that) you'd expect to transform back without any hassle at some point.<br /> If someone transformed me into a hound with monster-surgery... yeah, that's not something you recover from. The difference is night and day. The literal meanings of the words 'protean' and 'vicissitude' imply very different things too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Protean discipline powers that we know are reversible. The Protean discipline powers that we know aren't capable of making some of the changes displayed in the art for the upcoming Companion or the work of the Butterfly in <i>Anarch</i>. The victims of the latter weren't recovering and it was described as mutilation. Either the scope of Protean is broader than what you say it is and that the name implies or they're using something other than Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T02:40:25-08:00","id":1426808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426708#post1426708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why one 12th generation Tzimisce in Tokyo in the 21st century should deeply care about a war in medieval Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>12th gen? Dawkins wtf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> was Fiorenza also Dawkins' idea?<br /> <br /> anyway, the issue is the fact that Tzimisce just casually let one of their 12th gen dirty their name,<br /> and Tzimisce have been the most active cainite clan in Tokyo,<br /> so no excuse for their negligence<br /> <br /> it would've made more sense if that Tzimisce Prince masqueraded as a Ventrue to avoid their clan's attention<br /> <br /> remember that Lasombra had to murder their elders (well, actually neonates they framed as elders) to move to the Camarilla<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T12:44:43-08:00","id":1426848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426808#post1426808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">remember that Lasombra had to murder their elders (well, actually neonates they framed as elders) to move to the Camarilla</div> </div> </div> </div>That's silly on top of silly on top of more silly.<br /> <br /> I like the Antis.<br /> I played an anti. It was great.<br /> This metaplot change would totally fuck shit up for him. Both from a character perspective and a narrative one. It's also just... Really unrealistic? Did the Vauldrie actually stop being a thing? Are there even enough lasombra to be pulling off this nonsense? Aren't the Camarilla moving into old Sabbat territory so really the Lasombra are just handing them a lot of Domain? Must the most -IGetShitDone clan become a bunch of toadies?<br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose the Sabbat would beat the Cam physically because it doesn't actually want the Lasombra and the huge territories they're offering snag-free and the Cam doesn't have Brujah now. Like the Brujah would ever agree to let that happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T12:59:18-08:00","id":1426851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426848#post1426848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the Vauldrie actually stop being a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the devs realized the vinculum was too strong a plot device and had to get rid of it,<br /> but then they introduced the book of the grave war and...well I'm confused<br /> <br /> while I don't think a break from the sabbat would be entirely impossible, it bothers me how fast everything seemed to happen,<br /> I'm not entirely sure, but it seems like in a short periode of time (by vampire standards), gehenna happened, the camarilla and anarchs restructured, they rekt the sabbat, the lasombra broke off, they murdered all Cardinals, they re-established the masquerade without use of technology, they established blood cults that seem like they've always been there etc<br /> <br /> I mean, man, take a break, this ain't a marathon, vampires are supposed to take it slow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T13:05:52-08:00","id":1426854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra are just handing them a lot of Domain? Must the most -IGetShitDone clan become a bunch of toadies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know! It breaks there character so damn much it doesn't make sense. Actual Lasombra pre-V5 would never let any of this crap go down on a massive scale. It would be a huge stain on their pedigree not even talking to account their basic principle (Path).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T15:55:29-08:00","id":1426871,"title":"","content":"Clans aren't sports teams. I don't think clan is as unimportant as said in the Revised Vampire Player's Guide, but I do think that assigning a single personality and set of goals to an entire clan is downright weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T20:24:03-08:00","id":1426903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426848#post1426848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't the Camarilla moving into old Sabbat territory so really the Lasombra are just handing them a lot of Domain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, Giangaleazzo's defection was a thing. The fact that no one thought to try 'the Milan model' for luring tired Lasombra away from the Sabbat on a wider scale is baffling. The Camarilla gets more territory and competent leaders, the Lasombra get to switch teams while retaining authority and power with a minimum of ego-bruising, everyone wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T20:58:58-08:00","id":1426913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra get to switch teams while retaining authority and power with a minimum of ego-bruising,</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? You really think that the Lasombra will have ANY authority in the Camarilla AT ALL? Their main rival, the Venture that controls it, will just keep them as pity trophies that signal their victory over the Lasombra. The Sabbat was basically the BABY of the Lasombra and to see it go to tatters like this a MASSIVE prestation hit they will never recover from. Calling V5 Lasombra &quot;comptetent&quot; is also very generous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T21:05:57-08:00","id":1426914,"title":"","content":"In Shadows of New York, it's pretty clear Lasombra aren't trusted or given much power, and the demand for one Lasombra's destruction for each Lasombra who joins is definitely punitive. I know in VRev Lasombra Antitribu had joined the Camarilla, but the ex-Sabbat looking to shelter in the Camarilla do not have an easy time. I'm not sure the ones who were already in the Camarilla are having an easy time at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:01:34-08:00","id":1426933,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know how it is with joining the Antitribu by non-Sabbat Vampires? Are they considered to be Antitribu upon joining the Sabbat and participating in the Ritae, or are they treated like second-class members? I assume there must be a distinction because for example the Toreador Weakness probably stays the same, but on the other hand, Sabbat can't really afford to treat converts badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:13:42-08:00","id":1426937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426903#post1426903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, Giangaleazzo's defection was a thing. The fact that no one thought to try 'the Milan model' for luring tired Lasombra away from the Sabbat on a wider scale is baffling. The Camarilla gets more territory and competent leaders, the Lasombra get to switch teams while retaining authority and power with a minimum of ego-bruising, everyone wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>the sabbat weren't going to fall for that twice,<br /> in Archons and Templars, it explicitly stated how the sabbat had grown more distrustful since the Milan disaster and the Assamite betrayal<br /> <br /> what would really baffle me is the sudden change of attitude between Revised and V20/V5,<br /> in Revised, the sabbat had gone to the extreme, trusting no-one and even filtering problem factions off their ranks (tal'mahe'ra, the harmonists etc)<br /> <br /> but later editions, they just sort of relaxed their tensions,<br /> imo, it would've made more sense if the lasombra defectors were kicked out,<br /> instead, the defectors just walked out leaving a big mess on the way out,<br /> you'd think the sabbat would have learned the lesson by now but...I guess not<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:24:19-08:00","id":1426939,"title":"","content":"I think in V20 that had to do with creating an homage to all previous editions without much reference to the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:27:10-08:00","id":1426940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426939#post1426939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in V20 that had to do with creating an homage to all previous editions without much reference to the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>by V20, I meant BJD,<br /> though admittedly, some of the sabbat events in BJD might have been influenced by the V5 devs to link BJD to the V5 metaplot,<br /> but I'm not sure<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T04:34:16-08:00","id":1426953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426933#post1426933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how it is with joining the Antitribu by non-Sabbat Vampires? Are they considered to be Antitribu upon joining the Sabbat and participating in the Ritae, or are they treated like second-class members? I assume there must be a distinction because for example the Toreador Weakness probably stays the same, but on the other hand, Sabbat can't really afford to treat converts badly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For most clans, you're the Antitribe just by joining the Sabbat. But not for every clan.<br /> The Nosferatu are mostly nominal sect members either way. they're just playing up their loyalty with titles like antitribu<br /> The Tremere get the mark of the betrayer the moment they taste a vauldrie. <br /> The Ventrue who join the Sabbat have to go through a ritual to be a 'proper' Ventrue anti. Namely replace Presence with Auspex. I'd imagine the Brujah/Tzmisce/Lasombra would see them as threats if they didn't.<br /> The Assamite Antitribu shook off their -weakness to Vitae- Tremere curse, or avoided it, Assamites who joined during the Tremere curse/Before Ur-Shulgi wouldn't automaticaly shake of that curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T04:53:23-08:00","id":1426955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426953#post1426953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For most clans, you're the Antitribe just by joining the Sabbat. But not for every clan.<br /> The Nosferatu are mostly nominal sect members either way. they're just playing up their loyalty with titles like antitribu<br /> The Tremere get the mark of the betrayer the moment they taste a vauldrie.<br /> The Ventrue who join the Sabbat have to go through a ritual to be a 'proper' Ventrue anti. Namely replace Presence with Auspex. I'd imagine the Brujah/Tzmisce/Lasombra would see them as threats if they didn't.<br /> The Assamite Antitribu shook off their -weakness to Vitae- Tremere curse, or avoided it, Assamites who joined during the Tremere curse/Before Ur-Shulgi wouldn't automaticaly shake of that curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see.<br /> The Tremere converts probably have to go through some initiation into House Goratrix. <br /> The Malkavians most likely end up having their Dominate swapped for Dementation, if this hasn't happened yet.<br /> I thought that in Revised the Ventrue Antitribu have Presence. But going with that they have Auspex, Is it written anywhere how a ritual that changes Disciplines looks like? The only similar situation I recall is the relatively simple &quot;Smile widely and madly for a moment&quot; way Dementation is spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T07:13:18-08:00","id":1426974,"title":"","content":"So quick aside, do you think the Lasombra Submarine is still a thing by modern nights or do you think they Sank it by now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T07:21:17-08:00","id":1426977,"title":"","content":"Anyone wealthy enough can buy their own luxury submarine these days, but that's in the realm of a couple billion dollars or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T14:23:18-08:00","id":1427200,"title":"","content":"I have to approach the question from a metanarrative/setting perspective as opposed to anything &quot;realistic&quot;. In my view, the reason why the Camarilla and Sabbat exist in the setting is to allow two very different conceptions of vampires to be played. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla exists to allow more modern style vampires - the kind of vampires that exist hidden among humanity found in Anne Rice, Whitley Streiber's the Hunger, the Lost Boys, and other modern takes. As well as depictions of more humane vampires who struggle through their condition - Louis, Hannibal King, Nick Knight, etc. Although bloodsuckers, these vampires typically appear human, infiltrate through human society unrecognized, and spend a lot of effort keeping their nature a secret. If you want to tell these kinds of stories, you need something like the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat exists to portray more traditional vampires - the vampire who shows up and immediately starts turning others into vampires left and right like a plague. A lot of Dracula movies are like this (although he also fits into the above mold as well) as are derivatives in Hammer Horror movies, Count Yorga, Salem's Lot, etc. These are more monstrous vampires who are actively malevolent and blasphemous.<br /> <br /> Both types of vampires are interesting, both can be fun to play, but both are very different portrayals.<br /> <br /> So if the Sabbat wins, we eliminate the first type and only the second type exist (or at least dominates). That leads to a very different kind of setting and story. If we want to preserve a kind of Masquerade so humanity doesn't know about vampires as a whole, it probably means most vampires are destroyed and there are active hunter organizations who take care of that. Or that the Sabbat is merciless about vampires who &quot;endanger&quot; their fellow Cainites by their foolish actions, and we get an even more draconian Masquerade. Or we could say the Masquerade implodes and the knowledge of vampires gets out into the public which means a vastly different kind of setting. At that point it is either outright war between humanity and vampires, or vampires somehow subjugate humanity and we get something like Kim Newman's Anno Dracula series. Maybe there are other variations I'm not thinking of right now.<br /> <br /> So it all depends on what kind of setting you want, and what kind of plots and stories you want to tell as an ST and have your PCs experience. Everything else is just details or contrivances to get you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T14:40:28-08:00","id":1427204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426933#post1426933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how it is with joining the Antitribu by non-Sabbat Vampires? Are they considered to be Antitribu upon joining the Sabbat and participating in the Ritae, or are they treated like second-class members? I assume there must be a distinction because for example the Toreador Weakness probably stays the same, but on the other hand, Sabbat can't really afford to treat converts badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume there remains the distinction between &quot;False Sabbat&quot; versus &quot;True Sabbat&quot;. You're not True Sabbat until the Creation Rite is applied to you, and that only happens when you prove yourself. Sabbat won't perform the Creation Rites on any defectors to their sect until they've done something that proves their loyalty to the sect and its ideals. That's mainly a pack thing, and each pack likely has its own criteria on when it gets performed. I believe most False Sabbat get destroyed in war against the Sabbat's enemies before they ever have the chance of becoming True Sabbat. An important enough defector, probably plans his defection well in advance and does so in a way that probably allows him to receive the Creation Rites immediately upon defection. But ordinary schmuck vampires? They're in for hell.<br /> <br /> The different clan weakness and discpline sets of the original Player's Guide is an artifact of its times, when almost every bloodline had its own special thing, and there was a new bloodline every other book. There isn't an in-game reason for it. There's no reason to carry that over unless you like that sort of thing. If you do like, either handwave it away or come up with your own explanation that sounds good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T04:02:27-08:00","id":1427260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1427204#post1427204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume there remains the distinction between &quot;False Sabbat&quot; versus &quot;True Sabbat&quot;. You're not True Sabbat until the Creation Rite is applied to you, and that only happens when you prove yourself. Sabbat won't perform the Creation Rites on any defectors to their sect until they've done something that proves their loyalty to the sect and its ideals. That's mainly a pack thing, and each pack likely has its own criteria on when it gets performed. I believe most False Sabbat get destroyed in war against the Sabbat's enemies before they ever have the chance of becoming True Sabbat. An important enough defector, probably plans his defection well in advance and does so in a way that probably allows him to receive the Creation Rites immediately upon defection. But ordinary schmuck vampires? They're in for hell.<br /> <br /> The different clan weakness and discpline sets of the original Player's Guide is an artifact of its times, when almost every bloodline had its own special thing, and there was a new bloodline every other book. There isn't an in-game reason for it. There's no reason to carry that over unless you like that sort of thing. If you do like, either handwave it away or come up with your own explanation that sounds good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the Creation Rites, I had the feeling I was missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T14:00:55-08:00","id":1427298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1426977#post1426977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone wealthy enough can buy their own luxury submarine these days, but that's in the realm of a couple billion dollars or so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Google says they range from $60,000 for the low end up to 80 million for a 5,000 sq ft with living and dining room. The military spend 2+billion per sub, but I think something could be found in just about any vampires price range. I had a friend who was saving up for a personal sub, then he got married <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T14:59:43-08:00","id":1427304,"title":"","content":"Somehow the idea of (Lasombra) Vampires <i>stealing</i> a submarine appeals to me more than outright buying one. A bought one can be (much) more easily traced, after all, so that's one advantage stealing has here.<br /> Also stealing a submarine seems to me the kind of event that can be used to leave all kinds of interesting (false) leads that might lure into traps any persons attempting to find the submarine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-04-2020, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T15:11:45-08:00","id":1427306,"title":"","content":"They could always realistically buy such a thing on the black-market. Or maybe like you say, steal it, then sell it for a profit on said market; after waiting for awhile to deal it once the heat surrounding it dies down of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T16:07:05-08:00","id":1427311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1427306#post1427306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could always realistically buy such a thing on the black-market. Or maybe like you say, steal it, then sell it for a profit on said market; after waiting for awhile to deal it once the heat surrounding it dies down of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have some certain information that there are submarines for sale on the black market? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T03:07:39-08:00","id":1427343,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine they just got it from some corruption. <br /> <br /> Hey Igor, the papers say twelve subs were made, why do I only count eleven? <br /> Oh, it's off for maintenance/ we scrapped it because it was faulty/ We sold it to the CIA / That's a typo, let me correct that for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T06:04:24-08:00","id":1427352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1417835-what-if-the-sabbat-beat-the-camarilla?p=1427343#post1427343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine they just got it from some corruption.<br /> <br /> Hey Igor, the papers say twelve subs were made, why do I only count eleven?<br /> Oh, it's off for maintenance/ we scrapped it because it was faulty/ We sold it to the CIA / That's a typo, let me correct that for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explains it, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}